  <h2>{cas.maturity}</h2>
  <p>Module revision {cas.revision} · How an attack close to friendly troops is controlled and briefed: who the <Term>JTAC</Term> and the <Term>FAC(A)</Term> are and who holds which part of the job, the three types of control and the two methods of attack, the check-in, game plan and <Term>9-line</Term> brief with its readbacks, marks and talk-ons, and the rules that keep bombs off friendly troops. Written for fixed- and rotary-wing aircrew of every service from the joint close air support publication, which the Air Force, Army, Marine Corps and Navy all follow.</p>
